{{!-- SECTION / TYPE. The section half carries the desk colour.

     The type is the first public tag after the desk that is not itself
     a desk. A story tagged Technology and then Philosophy is not an
     essay of type "Philosophy": it is a Technology story that also
     touches the other desk, and reading the second desk as a type
     printed TECHNOLOGY / PHILOSOPHY, which claims something the editor
     never said. Both desks are skipped when looking for the type.

     foreach cannot stop at the first match, so every candidate is
     printed and CSS shows the first. The separator lives on the part
     rather than beside it, so it cannot exist without the word after
     it: a lone slash above a headline is structurally impossible here.

     No tag is ever linked. The whole card is already a link, and an
     anchor inside an anchor makes the browser close the outer one
     early, which silently drops the headline out of the link.

     foreach excludes internal tags by default, so #this-week and its
     kind can never surface. --}}

{{#if primary_tag}}<span class="lc-label"><b>{{primary_tag.name}}</b>{{#foreach tags from="2"}}{{#match slug "!=" "technology"}}{{#match slug "!=" "philosophy"}}<span class="lc-label-part">{{name}}</span>{{/match}}{{/match}}{{/foreach}}</span>{{/if}}
